{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791103739,"nonce":"1RnmwHvmg/1LFtgKCBsqf2sifZo=","title":"Pool workers re-enter the single interpreter through closure_runner and corrupt its frames","message":"Reported by chimpmonk-03 (ChimpMonk git-bug 830f4b7). Eight FixedThreadPool\njobs each building a DodgeEnv at once abort 3 out of 3:\n\n    thread 'ash-vm-3' panicked at crates/ash_interp/src/frame.rs:220:9:\n    cannot write register 12: the frame holds 0, and was built for function index 903 ...\n\nReproducer: /Users/amaterasu/Vibranium/chimpmonk/repro/ash_threads/run.sh\n(`build` mode).\n\nCause: a worker lane (every ash-vm-N thread) running a closure whose function\nis not compiled yet goes hlp_jit_closure_runner -\u003e hlp_call_method, which hands\nan unbound sentinel closure (and any bound closure) to\ncrate::fiber::closure_runner() -- the one interpreter on the main scheduler. Two\nworkers in it share its frame stack. The stub bridge and run_closure already\nrefuse worker lanes; these std paths did not ask. (\"holds 0\" is the write\npath's hard-coded length, not the frame's real size.)","files":null}]}